body:
Implements the current OCC-side half of the uploaded memory → qualification package against current main and the already-merged studious-pancake bridge.

What this PR adds:
- opt-in Native Messaging command `qualification.inspect`, disabled by default;
- fixed operator-owned Python/adapter/profile paths, never supplied by Chrome/model/source content;
- a fail-closed Python adapter that verifies a clean exact OCC SHA and invokes only `studious-pancake/scripts/run_occ_memory_qualification.py`;
- bounded source references (`source_id`, `version`, SHA256) as metadata only;
- replay-safe OCC receipts and reconciliation-required state after unknown/interrupted child outcomes;
- strict validation that bot results remain `qualified=false`, `release_authorized=false`, `live_authorized=false`, and `transactions_sent=0`;
- installer copies the new bridge files but does not enable them automatically;
- cross-platform deterministic CI now runs the Python adapter regression in addition to existing native tests;
- Russian operator/runbook documentation and profile/request examples.

This intentionally does not add a second scheduler/qualification engine, UI permissions, signer/wallet access, Laya/LLM inference, or trading authority.

The old draft #12 is not merged: it diverged 47 commits from current main and depended on obsolete studious-pancake draft #547. This PR supersedes that adapter with the current #554 contract.

Local isolated validation before publication:
- Python adapter: 7/7 tests passed.
- Qualification Native bridge: 7/7 tests passed.
- Python compile and Node syntax checks passed.
